---
const faqs = [
  { q: 'Is there a detox for meth?', a: "Usually not a separate one. Meth does not put the body in the kind of danger that alcohol or benzodiazepines do when they stop, so treatment normally begins with residential care rather than a detox stay. If you are also using fentanyl, other opioids or alcohol, then a supervised detox does come first — and that happens in the same building." },
  { q: 'Does AHCCCS cover it?', a: "Access covers residential treatment, and it is how a great many people here are funded. Banner University Family Care is in network with us, and further plan contracts are being added. Give us the plan name on your card and we will check it while you are on the phone." },
  { q: "I'm using fentanyl as well. Can you still take me?", a: "Yes, and that combination is a very familiar one. It usually means starting with a medically supervised detox for the fentanyl before moving into residential treatment, both under the same roof and as one admission." },
  { q: 'How long would I be there?', a: "Residential stays are commonly around thirty days, and often somewhat longer where a plan authorises it. What you need is decided with your case manager rather than fixed in advance." },
  { q: 'Will I be able to sleep?', a: "Yes, and a great deal of it in the first few days. Arriving exhausted is the norm and the schedule accommodates it. Rest is treated as part of the recovery rather than something to get through before the real work starts." },
  { q: 'What about my job?', a: "Bring it up on the first call. Plenty of people arrive having arranged protected leave, and knowing your timing lets us plan the stay around it where that is possible." },
  { q: 'I have court dates or probation.', a: "Say so early. Legal obligations are common among the people we treat and they can usually be worked around — your case manager can help with documentation and scheduling while you are with us." },
  { q: "I've been to treatment before and it didn't stick.", a: "Then you already know more about this than someone arriving for the first time. Coming back is the ordinary shape of recovery for a lot of people, and there is no limit on how many times you are allowed to try." },
];
---
<section id="meth-faq" class="bg-cream py-[70px]">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <p class="text-gold font-body text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.18em] uppercase mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
      <span class="w-6 h-px bg-gold inline-block"></span>
      Straight answers
    </p>
    <h2 class="font-display text-charcoal mb-10">Questions worth asking</h2>

    <div class="divide-y divide-cream-soft border-t border-b border-cream-soft">
      {faqs.map(f => (
        <details class="group py-5">
          <summary class="flex items-start justify-between gap-6 cursor-pointer">
            <h3 class="font-body font-semibold text-charcoal text-[18px] leading-[28px]">{f.q}</h3>
            <span class="shrink-0 mt-1 text-teal">
              <svg class="faq-plus w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/>
              </svg>
              <svg class="faq-minus w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" d="M5 12h14"/>
              </svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <p class="font-body text-charcoal text-[16px] leading-[27px] mt-4 pr-10">{f.a}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
